  "name": null,
  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<1.08).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1230\\,$ | $\\,0.1210\\,$ | $\\,0.1192\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1446\\,$ | $\\,0.1423\\,$ | $\\,0.1401\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1685\\,$ | $\\,0.1660\\,$ | $\\,0.1635\\,$ |\n\n$P(Z<1.08)=$\n{{field-1}}",
